\nflash flooding in and around the Gold Mountain Burn Scar.\n\nSOURCE...Public reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nGold Mountain Burn Scar.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nHighway 550 from Portland to Ouray and over the Gold Mountain burn\nscar.","ends":"2026-09-17T03:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Gunnison, CO; Hinsdale, CO; Ouray, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.73f0b275b56d4aba42806388f0ca716585d67d6f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.73f0b275b56d4aba42806388f0ca716585d67d6f.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued September 16 at 9:39AM MDT until September 18 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River,\nNorthwest San Juan Mountains, San Juan River Basin and Southwest\nSan Juan Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...Through Thursday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nThis also includes the Gold Mountain, Elk and Ferris burn scars as\nwell as areas of steep, susceptible terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Recent heavy rainfall in southwest Colorado has led to already\nsaturated ground. In addition, multiple rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms are expected Wednesday afternoon through Thursday\nevening producing periods of heavy rainfall and potential flash\nflooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-18T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d0f7f9a5a0805fda6f1988fda5f919f56cf2d735.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d0f7f9a5a0805fda6f1988fda5f919f56cf2d735.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-17T04:50:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 170450 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1050 PM MDT Wed Sep 16 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flash flooding will be possible for the coming days as record moisture propagates through eastern Utah and western Colorado. - Flood Watches remain in effect for SE Utah and SW Colorado today through Thursday. - Impacts from flash flooding could observed ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-16T18:50:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Sub-tropical moisture continues to propagate through the area which is feeding shower and thunderstorm activity through the end of the week. These storms bring a threat of heavy rainfall and potential for excess runoff, especially over burn scars. Because widespread wetting rainfall is expected over the next several days, the threat of critical fire weather conditions is eliminated ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":null,"aviation":{"icao":"KASE","distance_km":36.2,"raw_metar":"METAR KASE 170453Z AUTO 34003KT 10SM -RA SCT065 OVC080 13/11 A3045 RMK AO2 RAB34 SLP198 P0000 T01280106","temp_f":55,"wind_dir":340,"wind_kt":3,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":"OVC","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1031.2,"observed":1789620780,"raw_taf":"TAF KASE 162321Z 1700/1724 15006KT P6SM VCSH SCT060 OVC100 PROB30 1700/1706 -TSRA BKN050CB OVC080 FM170600 VRB03KT P6SM VCSH BKN050 BKN080 TEMPO 1706/1710 -SHRA OVC025 FM171000 15003KT P6SM -SHRA BKN035 BKN050 FM171700 10006KT P6SM -RA BKN040 OVC060 PROB30 1718/1724 -TSRA BKN035CB OVC050","url":"https://aviationweather.gov/data/metar/?ids=KASE&hours=0"},"airgradient":null,"airnow":{"aqi":14,"category":"Good","parameter":"O3","r